<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Sheikhdom of Sancul</h1><p class="st-meta">1700 CE – 1910 CE (approx.) · capital Sancul</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Swahili Muslim sheikhdom on the mainland opposite Mozambique Island, alternately ally and rival of the Portuguese.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Sancul developed on the coast south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique-island">Mozambique Island</a> as a settlement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> Muslim families, many connected to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-angoche">Angoche</a> and other coastal towns. By the 18th century it was governed by its own sheikhs, who held land and authority over neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/makua">Makua</a> communities.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The sheikhs combined Islamic leadership with control of trade between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/makua">Makua</a> interior and the coast. They sometimes allied with the Portuguese at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique-island">Mozambique Island</a> and sometimes resisted their demands. In the 19th century Sancul profited from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comoro-islands">Comoros</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> and the French islands.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Sancul joined the coastal resistance to Portuguese occupation in the late 19th century. Portuguese campaigns against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> sheikhdoms and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-angoche">Sultanate of Angoche</a> brought it under colonial control by 1910.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1700 CE – 1910 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:93.53%;width:4.18%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1700 CE – 1910 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sancul</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Swahili, Makua</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mozambique">Mozambique</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sancul</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1805&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-sancul" aria-label="Sheikhdom of Sancul on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5710 2684 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sheikhdom of Sancul lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5861 3386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6030 2940h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M6030 2940h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Mozambique. <a href="/atlas?year=1805&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-sancul">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

